    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you on the income thing, but some of the council members are pushing back. They're arguing that \"equity\" should actually mean maximizing the total impact of the housing—like, making sure the units go to the people who will actually use the transit and drive economic growth for the city, not just the lowest earners. They think a lottery or transit-proximate model is more \"fair\" to the community as a whole. \n\nDoesn't that approach count as equitable too? How do you reconcile that with your recommendation?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
